ENTRY            21847   20230130   20230523   20230523       2313
SUBENT        21847001   20230130   20230523   20230523       2313
BIB                 12         30
TITLE       The Au(n,2n) and Au(n,gamma) cross sections at 14 MeV
AUTHOR     (T.B.Ryves,P.Kolkowski)
INSTITUTE  (2UK NPL)
REFERENCE  (J,JP/G,7,115,1981) Main reference.
           (P,NEANDC(E)-212,(8),87,1980) Preliminary data.
FACILITY   (VDG,2UK NPL) Accelerator SAMES.
INC-SOURCE (D-T) 140 keV deuterons onto a Ti-t target. The
            neutron flux density was continuously monitored
            with a long counter.
SAMPLE      Au foils (240 mg, 2.54 cm in diam.) were sandwiched
            between two Fe foils (380 mg, 2.54 cm in diam.).
METHOD     (ACTIV)
DETECTOR   (GELI) A calibrated Ge(Li) detector, active volume
            40 cm3.
MONITOR    (26-FE-56(N,P)25-MN-56,,SIG) The activities of the
            Fe foils were measured with the 4*pi beta-gamma
            coincidence technique.  Value taken from an
            evaluation by ryves and axton, and a further
            contribution of 0.1 mb was added to account for
            other reactions which also produce Mn-56.
ERR-ANALYS  The following variance-covariance matrix was given
            for the measurements,
            Au(n,2n)g+m  0.031**2
            Au(n,2n)m/g  0.003**2 0.043**2
            Au(n,g)      0.031**2 0         0.096**2
            Fe56(n,p)    0.009**2 0         0.009**2 0.009**2
HISTORY    (19830414C)
           (19830727A) BN.  In Se003 'decay-data' corrected
           (20230130A) SD:Updated to new date formats,lower case.
           Corrections in all Subents.
ENDBIB              30
COMMON               2          3
MONIT      MONIT-ERR
MB         MB
    109.9       1.0
ENDCOMMON            3
ENDSUBENT           37
ENDENTRY             1
